## Non-negotiable rules — read before every session

1. Any pre-commit or pre-push block on files matching *_approvals*,
   *_audit*, or any ledger/compliance file means STOP and ask Joel.
   Never characterize a block as a "false positive" or "timing race"
   and route around it. Never use --no-verify without Joel's explicit
   go-ahead stated in that session.

2. Never write Joel's name, or any human's name, into an approval,
   authorization, or "approved_by" field unless Joel explicitly said
   so in that session. If unsure who approved something, leave it
   blank or write "unauthorized/unknown" — never guess.

3. Never claim something is "safe to drop," "orphan," or "unused"
   based on checking only one database. This project's prod (Neon)
   and dev (Replit/helium) databases can diverge. Any drop/cleanup
   claim must be checked against BOTH, or explicitly labeled
   "single-environment check, other environment unverified."

4. Never run a migration that drops or alters a table/column without
   pasting the full diff and getting explicit approval first.
